 looking for to  know that that's the only thing we're  doing  we've got crews there that you know  we've been going from seven to seven and  seven to seven and we'll keep going  until we get everybody who can be pulled  out pulled out of that building  uh it's amazing the resources that we've  been given  president biden the white house our two  senators rubio and scott  our governor who's been here debbie  wasserman schultz in the dade county  mayor cava have given us resources which  have overwhelmed us  we've actually probably got too many  resources but we don't have a resource  problem we've got a love problem we just  need to be able to focus  we need a little good weather we need a  couple good breaks  and that's that's really what we need  because we've got everything else  we just and we've also got the intention  to stay here and get the job done  mayor we know an essential part of the  search and rescue operation  is dogs who sniff out signs of life  yesterday you told us that the dogs had  zero hits  as they scrambled over the rubble any  updates today on that front  well you know i i was at it two in the  morning last night the dogs came at  about four or five i think  and they didn't have zero hits but they  had a few hits  uh you know we found the little boy and  and the woman  but uh uh it's been tough the rain makes  it tough  uh the fire certainly makes it tough um  but that doesn't mean that the search  doesn't  continue so we're going to do everything  we can  we're going to hope mother nature  cooperates and  you know we're going to just do  everything we can yeah that's the bottom  line and i want  absolutely go ahead i notice there's a  crane  over your left shoulder uh doing work on  what appears to be the top of the rubble  or is that crane taking things off the  side of the building what's that  operation we see  that that that crane is there because  apparently there were  dangerous pieces of rubble that were  possibly  likely to fall on 